Generates synthetic longitudinal data with a conditional temporal VAE (LSTM encoder/decoder).
This file only defines the generator; the data are generated in the files that use it
(PART 2 — Corsano data, PART 3 — PBC and the other test datasets). **CHANGED:** the Corsano generation moved to PART 2.

Input: a data frame with `patient_id`, a time column (`time_var`) and variable columns; nothing else to choose.
What the generator handles: unequal and irregular visits (visit grid from `time_var`), missing values
(masked in the loss, missingness reproduced), patient traits found automatically (variables constant within
patient) used as conditioning, Box-Cox + standardization, KL warm-up, z drawn given the traits,
noise with the real structure (patient-level intercept/slope + day-to-day correlation), persistent draws for
time-varying categories, and output on the observed scale (no NaN, observed bounds, discrete values kept).
Changes from the original code are marked `# NEW` / `# CHANGED`. Fixes 1–4 refer to the validation in PART 3.

